{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"REJECT\n### VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n- `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lalal.py tests/test_separation.py`: 26 passed\n- Static review: each original-source operation owns separate `backend_state`; `LalalSeparator.split()` consequently calls `/upload/` once per operation instead of reusing one original `source_id`.\n- Static review: `preflight()` uses only local `soundfile` duration and permits `needed == 0`; it never checks the upload response’s authoritative duration before submission.\n\n### VERDICT REASON\nThe implementation must persist and share the original upload across vocals/bass/drums/guitar, then upload the instrumental once for the cascade—two uploads total. It must also make preflight cost-safe for every supported source: derive the outstanding-operation sum from authoritative uploaded durations (including the instrumental cascade) and refuse all paid submissions when duration cannot be established or credits are insufficient. Add mocked regression tests for both cases."}}
